# cloudflared tunnel config — MVR rig PC
# Windows location (service): C:\Users\<you>\.cloudflared\config.yml
# After editing: cloudflared service uninstall / install, or restart the
# "Cloudflared agent" Windows service so it rereads this file.
#
# Replace <TUNNEL-ID> with your tunnel's UUID (see `cloudflared tunnel list`).

tunnel: <TUNNEL-ID>
credentials-file: C:\Users\russ\.cloudflared\<TUNNEL-ID>.json

ingress:
  # Named machine -> the local MCC DAQ server. WebSockets pass through
  # automatically, so live charts work.
  - hostname: mvr1.keenmvr.com
    service: http://localhost:8000

  # (Later) a second machine on ANOTHER PC gets its OWN tunnel + config with
  # hostname mvr2.keenmvr.com. If a second server ever runs on THIS PC on a
  # different port, add it here instead:
  # - hostname: mvr2.keenmvr.com
  #   service: http://localhost:8001

  # Required catch-all: anything not matched above gets a 404.
  - service: http_status:404
